###Setting up a proportion

Corresponding sides of similar triangles are proportional, so we can set up and solve a proportion: 

$\dfrac{\blueE{BL}}{BS}=\dfrac{AL}{TS}$

We picked side $\blueE{\overline{BL}}$ because we need to find its length.

We picked side $\overline{BS}$ because it corresponds to side $\blueE{\overline{BL}}$.

Then we picked another pair of corresponding sides where we already knew the measurements.

$\begin{array}{rcl}
&\triangle BAL
\\
{\text{opposite to } \atop \angle A/\angle T}
&\overbrace{\underbrace{\!\!\!\!\!\left\{ 
\dfrac{\blueE{BL}}{BS}=\dfrac{AL}{TS}
\right\}\!\!\!\!\!}}
&{\text{opposite to } \atop \angle B}
\\
&\triangle BTS
\end{array}$
